      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Opportunity knocks at this most interesting property on Harold’s Cross Road, overlooking the park and positioned in one of Dublin’s most convenient south city locations. Requiring complete refurbishment and upgrading throughout, the property offers an exciting blank-canvas opportunity for cash buyers seeking a renovation project with real potential.\r\n\r\nExtending to approximately 105 sq. m, the accommodation was previously arranged as a three-bedroom house with two reception rooms. Subject to the necessary planning permissions, the property provides excellent scope to reconfigure, modernise and create a bespoke home tailored to individual requirements, finishes and specification.\r\n\r\nThe location is a key attraction, within walking distance of St Stephen’s Green and just a short stroll from the vibrant villages of Portobello and Rathmines, both offering an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, bars and local amenities. Griffith College and the Luas Red Line are also easily accessible, further enhancing the property’s appeal."
      },
